Zig is a general-purpose programming language and toolchain
for maintaining robust, optimal, and reusable software

The build supports i586, i686, and x86_64 Slackware systems.
Building the package may take some time because Zig is compiled from source
instead of using a precompiled binary.

The resulting package installs the compiler as /usr/bin/zig and its
runtime library files under /usr/lib/zig.
